+// ── 2a″. The union's two lines: the SWAP and line two's own rub-out (pass 8, §7's fence) ─
+//
+// HOLD's default path: a hint is answered (the record is held), the next hint displaces it, and
+// line one gives the record to line two in the same write. The old line-one node leaves as
+// `note-swap` (`animation: none`): a sentence displacing another is not an exit, and line two
+// already paints it, so that node must not outlive a frame or two. Pass 7's hook wrote the rung on
+// it and held it ~160 ms with the sentence on both lines for 16–20 frames (every gate green,
+// because the drop-clock rows read `.note-leave-active` only). This leg reads BOTH leaves of a
